      "source": [
        "# 01 - Vision PPE EDA\\n",
        "\\n",
        "## PPE detection framing\\n",
        "\\n",
        "SafetyOps Copilot processes **vision events** (images/frames) to estimate **PPE compliance**.\\n",
        "The goal is to detect whether persons in a scene are wearing required PPE such as hardhats and safety vests.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "For v1, we:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- Use a pre-trained YOLO model (`yolov8n`) via the `ultralytics` package.\\n",
        "- Implement a wrapper that computes a simple **compliance_score** in [0, 1].\\n",
        "- Fall back to a stub when YOLO is unavailable (e.g., CI, minimal dev environments)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Data and label format (YOLO-style)\\n",
        "\\n",
        "YOLO training typically expects labels in the following format per image:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- Text file per image with lines of:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "```text\\n",
        "<class_id> <x_center> <y_center> <width> <height>\\n",
        "```\\n",
        "\\n",
        "where coordinates are normalized to [0, 1] with respect to image width and height.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "For PPE detection, candidate classes might include:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- `person`\\n",
        "- `helmet` / `hardhat`\\n",
        "- `vest` / `safety_vest`\\n",
        "\\n",
        "We can:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- Start with generic COCO-trained models to detect `person`.\\n",
        "- Fine-tune or adjust heuristics for PPE-specific classes later.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "The repo does **not** include real training data; only small synthetic or placeholder references should live under `data/sample/`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Evaluation metrics\\n",
        "\\n",
        "For object detection and PPE compliance, we care about:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- **mAP (mean Average Precision)** at IoU thresholds (e.g., 0.5, 0.5:0.95).\\n",
        "- **Precision / Recall** per class (person, helmet, vest).\\n",
        "- **PPE compliance metrics** derived from detections, such as:\\n",
        "  - Fraction of persons with helmet and/or vest.\\n",
        "  - Rate of PPE violations by site, time, or task.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "When evaluating the compliance heuristic itself, we can treat it as a regression or thresholded classification task:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- Correlation between human-annotated compliance and model `compliance_score`.\\n",
        "- Accuracy / F1 for discrete compliance buckets (e.g., compliant vs non-compliant)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Qualitative error analysis plan\\n",
        "\\n",
        "Beyond aggregate metrics, **qualitative analysis** is crucial:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- Inspect images where:\\n",
        "  - The model misses obvious PPE.\\n",
        "  - The model hallucinates PPE that is not there.\\n",
        "- Look for systematic issues:\\n",
        "  - Camera angle and distance.\\n",
        "  - Lighting conditions.\\n",
        "  - Occlusions (e.g., people partly hidden).\\n",
        "  - Site-specific gear (e.g., different colored helmets or vests).\\n",
        "- Group errors by context:\\n",
        "  - Indoor vs outdoor.\\n",
        "  - Day vs night.\\n",
        "  - Site/region.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "These insights can drive data collection (e.g., capturing more examples of underrepresented scenarios) and model improvements (fine-tuning, augmentation strategies)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Compliance heuristic (v1)\\n",
        "\\n",
        "The v1 wrapper implemented in `safetyops.ml.vision.yolo.run_ppe_inference` uses a simple heuristic:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "1. Run YOLO on the image.\\n",
        "2. For each detection, map class ids to human-readable labels.\\n",
        "3. Count:\\n",
        "   - `num_persons`: detections labeled as person.\\n",
        "   - `num_persons_with_ppe`: person detections that also have helmet/vest around them (approximated by co-occurring detections).\\n",
        "4. Define `compliance_score = num_persons_with_ppe / max(num_persons, 1)`.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "If YOLO is unavailable, the wrapper logs a warning and returns a stub with a neutral score so that downstream components remain functional."
      ]
    },
